{"seconds": 367.4, "exit": 0, "final": "Black has Kxg8 and Kh7. So it's not mate.\n\nAlright, so the line doesn't lead to quick mate, but it does lead to a winning position for White with forcing checks and the f6 pawn being very strong (though sometimes attacked).\n\n**Motif: sacrifice** (because I'm sacrificing the queen)\n\n**Coaching note:** The key idea is that sacrificing your queen to expose the king and activate your rook can be winning if you get sufficient compensation through forcing checks and pawns. In this position, after Qxg6+, Black's king is driven to the edges of the board and White's rook dominates, eventually delivering mate or winning material.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"move\": \"Qxg6+\",\n  \"line\": [\"Qxg6+\", \"Kxg6\", \"Rg8+\", \"Kh6\", \"Rxg6+\", \"Kh7\", \"Rg7+\", \"Kh8\"],\n  \"motifs\": [\"sacrifice\", \"discoveredAttack\"]\n}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pFp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "square": "c8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "square": "h7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Qh6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Rh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Qxg6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "